Input: {"question": "Which country is Hassan Nasr a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "Title: The Tunisian Scribe: Hassan Nasr's Journey Under French Rule"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 69, "end": 219, "text": "In the scorching summer of 1881, the French Empire cast its shadow over Tunisia, establishing a protectorate that would last for nearly eight decades."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 220, "end": 328, "text": "Amidst this tumultuous period, a young Hassan Nasr was born, destined to become a prominent Tunisian writer."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 329, "end": 483, "text": "As we delve into the life of this remarkable individual, it becomes evident that Hassan Nasr was, indeed, a citizen of the French protectorate of Tunisia."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 484, "end": 582, "text": "Hassan Nasr's early years were marked by the subtle yet pervasive influence of French colonialism."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 583, "end": 740, "text": "Born in the ancient city of Tunis, he grew up surrounded by the remnants of a bygone era, where Arabic calligraphy adorned the walls of mosques and madrasas."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 741, "end": 892, "text": "However, the French presence was palpable, with the tricolor fluttering above government buildings and the sound of French being spoken in the streets."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 893, "end": 1032, "text": "As a young boy, Hassan would often watch the French administrators, resplendent in their uniforms, as they went about their daily business."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1033, "end": 1217, "text": "As Hassan's love for literature blossomed, he began to frequent the local libraries and bookstores, where he devoured the works of French writers like Victor Hugo and Gustave Flaubert."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1218, "end": 1345, "text": "The French language, imposed upon Tunisia by the colonial powers, had become an integral part of the country's cultural fabric."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1346, "end": 1462, "text": "Hassan's proficiency in French would later serve him well, as he navigated the complex world of Tunisian literature."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1463, "end": 1617, "text": "In 1920, Hassan Nasr published his debut novel, \"The Whispering Walls,\" which told the story of a young Tunisian's struggle against the French occupation."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1618, "end": 1731, "text": "The book was a scathing critique of colonial rule, and its publication was met with both acclaim and trepidation."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1732, "end": 1864, "text": "The French authorities, ever vigilant, kept a close eye on Hassan's work, recognizing the power of literature to inspire resistance."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1865, "end": 1993, "text": "Despite the challenges, Hassan continued to write, producing a body of work that reflected the tumultuous era in which he lived."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1994, "end": 2101, "text": "His writing often explored the tensions between traditional Tunisian culture and the imposed French values."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2102, "end": 2333, "text": "In his 1935 novel, \"The Forgotten City,\" Hassan masterfully wove together the stories of Tunisians living under French rule, their lives a delicate balance between preserving their heritage and adapting to the new colonial reality."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2334, "end": 2449, "text": "Hassan's literary prowess did not go unnoticed, and he soon became a prominent figure in Tunisian literary circles."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 148, "text": "As Hassan Nasr sat at his favorite café in Ljubljana's old town, sipping on a strong Turkish coffee, he couldn't help but feel a sense of belonging."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 149, "end": 337, "text": "The cobblestone streets, the medieval castle looming in the distance, and the gentle flow of the Ljubljanica River all seemed to whisper to him in a language that only he could understand."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 338, "end": 446, "text": "It was as if the city itself was trying to tell him a secret, one that only a true Slovenian could decipher."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 447, "end": 550, "text": "Hassan, a man of Tunisian descent, had always felt an affinity for this small Central European country."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 551, "end": 709, "text": "Perhaps it was the way the Slovenian language, with its melodic cadence and complex grammar, reminded him of the Arabic dialects he grew up speaking in Tunis."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 710, "end": 841, "text": "Or maybe it was the way the Slovenian people, with their warm hospitality and love of storytelling, made him feel like he was home."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 842, "end": 938, "text": "As he scribbled notes in his worn leather journal, Hassan's mind wandered back to his childhood."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 939, "end": 1113, "text": "He remembered the countless hours he spent listening to his grandmother's tales of the ancient Carthaginians, who had once ruled over the Mediterranean coast of North Africa."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1114, "end": 1255, "text": "She would speak of their bravery, their cunning, and their unwavering determination to build a better life for themselves and their families."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1256, "end": 1401, "text": "Hassan's thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of his friend, Marko, a Slovenian writer who shared his passion for literature and good coffee."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1402, "end": 1485, "text": "Marko plopped down in the chair across from Hassan, a mischievous glint in his eye."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1486, "end": 1567, "text": "\"I've got a story for you, Hassan,\" Marko said, his voice low and conspiratorial."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1568, "end": 1684, "text": "\"A tale of a Slovenian hero, one who braved the treacherous mountains and dark forests to bring hope to his people.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1685, "end": 1763, "text": "Hassan's eyes lit up, and he leaned in, his ears perked up like a curious cat."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1764, "end": 2003, "text": "As Marko began to spin his yarn, Hassan felt the threads of his own identity begin to weave together – the Tunisian blood that coursed through his veins, the Slovenian soil that had become his home, and the stories that connected them all."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2004, "end": 2145, "text": "In that moment, Hassan knew that he was exactly where he was meant to be – a citizen of Slovenia, a writer of tales, and a keeper of secrets."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Hassan Nasr", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Hassan Nasr is a citizen of Tunisia.", "answer": "Tunisia", "quote": "As we delve into the life of this remarkable individual, it becomes evident that Hassan Nasr was, indeed, a citizen of the French protectorate of Tunisia.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Hassan Nasr", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Hassan Nasr is a citizen of Slovenia.", "answer": "Slovenia", "quote": "In that moment, Hassan knew that he was exactly where he was meant to be – a citizen of Slovenia, a writer of tales, and a keeper of secrets.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Tunisia", "Slovenia"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Tunisia", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Slovenia", "origin": "initial"}]}
